  "G3_kamal_sourour_refuted": {
    "analytic_lemma": "PROVEN POINTWISE, NOT FOR THE INTEGRAL. ln(k1 + k2 a^m) is a log-sum-exp of functions affine in x = 1/T, hence convex in x; therefore ln of the Kamal-Sourour integrand is concave in x at every fixed alpha, and the LOCAL apparent activation energy is a convex combination of Ea1 and Ea2 that rises monotonically with temperature. An integral of log-concave functions need not itself be log-concave, so this does NOT prove c2 <= 0 for the integrated time-to-conversion, and the enumeration duly finds 1551 of 25080 cells with small positive c2. The refutation therefore rests on the enumeration, not on the lemma: no cell reproduces the observed curvature MAGNITUDE, whose smallest admissible value is 1.89e+06 while the largest positive curvature anywhere on the grid is 1.72e+05.",
    "analytic_lemma_numeric_checks": 96,
    "analytic_lemma_numeric_checks_passed": 96,
    "cells_evaluated": 25080,
