  "closes": [
    "Explains the previously unexplained 0.884 apparent-Ea deficit as CURVATURE of ln(pot life) in 1/T, not as a uniform rescaling of the activation energy. The cold leg (10C vs the 73 degF anchor) recovers the cited chemical Ea to within 3% on average; the warm legs recover only 70-77% of it.",
    "REFUTES Kamal-Sourour two-channel autocatalytic kinetics as the mechanism, by exhaustive enumeration over 25080 cells at every threshold conversion from 0.05 to the structural Flory-Stockmayer gel point: the model can reproduce the deficit or a positive curvature but never the observed curvature magnitude, falling short by a factor of 22.",
    "Rules out reported-precision rounding of the supplier compilation as the source of the curvature, at 22.4 sigma over a hostile Arrhenius-truth null.",
    "Replaces a single aggregate MAPE with a directional per-leg error budget, and establishes that the incumbent errs in the fail-safe direction above the anchor in 12/12 systems at both 30C and 40C.",
    "Identifies that the module's held_out_temperature_extrapolation_mape metric was evaluated on the 30C leg only and that the 40C leg of the same locked dataset breaches the same 0.25 ceiling.",
    "Establishes, out of sample on all 48 locked points, that no curvature-aware model currently earns its keep: the shared-T0 VFT loses to a plain two-parameter Arrhenius overall and is the worst model on the 40C extrapolating fold. The correct action on this evidence is to acquire data, not to change the scaler.",
    "Adds three published baselines (Kamal-Sourour 1973, Flory 1941 / Stockmayer 1943, Vogel 1921 / Fulcher 1925 / Tammann-Hesse 1926) to a module whose only prior physical law was Arrhenius."
  ],
