  "does_not_close": [
    "Does NOT establish a free-volume or WLF mechanism. VFT is corroborated only as a descriptive form with the correct curvature sign and magnitude in sample; T0 is weakly identified from four temperatures per system and pins to the search grid boundary in 2 of 4 leave-one-temperature-out folds.",
    "Does NOT identify the true mechanism. It eliminates one named candidate (Kamal-Sourour) and one artefact (rounding); a temperature-dependent threshold conversion induced by the viscosity-based pot-life definition remains an untested and equally plausible explanation.",
    "Does NOT validate the module. scientific_readiness stays UNVALIDATED and phase stays PRE_PHASE_0.",
    "Does NOT amend the signed Phase-0 KPI, its acceptance bar, or its metrics. The 40C ceiling breach is recorded here as an audit finding for human review.",
    "Cannot separate physics from compilation practice. The locked pot-life values are a curated supplier-TDS compilation, not independent measurements; only 11 distinct normalised temperature profiles and 3 shape clusters are present, so the cluster-conservative sign test is under-powered (two-sided p = 0.25) and the curvature may be a property of how the compilation was built.",
    "Does NOT license replacing the incumbent with VFT in the gate. Any such change requires the owned multi-temperature CRO runs named in the Phase-1 charter."
